course: dictionary
lesson: 11744
title: Slipping back: backsliding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Backsliding is a noun. It means going back to bad old habits after you had been doing better. Picture a car sliding backwards down a hill when it loses its grip: that is the idea to hold in your head.
explain: «After a week of healthy lunches, Sam started backsliding and ate crisps every day again.» The word «again» is a clue. Sam was doing well, then slipped back into the old habit.
explain: The verb is backslide, and it changes its form: backslides, backslid, backsliding. Church language uses the word too, for someone who turns away from their faith. The everyday meaning is the one you will meet most often.
fact: Backsliding means going back to bad old habits after you had been doing better.
fact: The past form of the verb backslide is backslid, as in «He backslid last winter and stopped going to the gym.»
fact: In church language, a «backslider» is someone who has turned away from their faith.
fact: Preachers in the 1800s used the word backslider often.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad promises to be good, then backslides as soon as he sees a motor car.
exercise: «After a week of healthy lunches, Sam started backsliding and ate crisps every day again.» What does backsliding mean here? | *Going back to an old bad habit after doing better | Sliding down a hill in the snow | Eating healthy food for the first time | Buying a big bag of crisps
exercise: «Last winter he backslid and stopped going to the gym.» Find and copy the past form of backslide. | backslide | backslides | backsliding | *backslid
exercise: «The preacher warned the church about backsliding.» In church language, what is a backslider? | *Someone who has turned away from their faith | Someone who lives in a faraway town | Someone who builds new churches | Someone who sings loudly in the choir
test: «Toad promised to be good, but he was backsliding within an hour.» What does backsliding mean? | Moving into a new house | Keeping a promise for a whole year | *Slipping back into bad old ways | Riding a bicycle very fast
test: Which sentence uses backsliding correctly? | «Backsliding is the colour of the sky.» | «Ben was backsliding his bicycle up the hill.» | «The backsliding sun rose over the hill.» | *«Ben was doing well at school, but his backsliding made his marks fall again.»
exam: «Ella kept her room tidy all month, but by the end of the summer she was backsliding.» What does the sentence tell us? | *Ella had been doing well, then slipped back into her old messy habits | Ella won a prize for the tidiest room | Ella never kept her room tidy at all | Ella moved house at the end of the summer
